WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.265
Each world you ride is kept on this device, so the next ride opens in seconds, even

00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:09.823
offline. This device shows what is kept.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.452
Saved worlds reads how many, how much space they take, and names them: three worlds,

00:00:15.452 --> 00:00:16.973
sixty-one megabytes.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.549
Clear saved worlds deletes them. The row reads None saved, and a toast says how much

00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:31.003
was freed, then closes on its own.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.051
Keep worlds after a ride is on by default. Turn it off, and nothing new is saved:

00:00:41.051 --> 00:00:43.780
the next ride downloads the world again.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:51.618
This device, from a phone to the full screen.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.390
And if the browser clears space on its own, World loading simply downloads the world

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.947
again. Nothing fails.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
